// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-26 | Modified: 2023-03-10
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001, G0069
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects suspicious command line patterns seen being used by MERCURY APT
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/08/25/mercury-leveraging-log4j-2-vulnerabilities-in-unpatched-systems-to-target-israeli-organizations/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2022/TA/MERCURY/proc_creation_win_apt_mercury.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-exec bypass -w 1 -enc" and ProcessCommandLine contains "UwB0AGEAcgB0AC0ASgBvAGIAIAAtAFMAYwByAGkAcAB0AEIAbABvAGMAawAgAHsAKABzAGEAcABzACAAKAAiAHAA"
